Subject: [PATCH] glib2: disable undeclared optional libelf dependency

GLib auto-detects libelf from an existing staging directory without declaring
an elfutils build dependency. A parallel rebuild can remove that library
before gresource links. Disable ELF resource inspection for gresource, a
utility not shipped by the target glib2 package, to keep the build independent
of staging contents and package build order.

--- a/feeds/packages/libs/glib2/Makefile
+++ b/feeds/packages/libs/glib2/Makefile
@@ -57,6 +57,9 @@ COMP_ARGS+=-Dlibmount=disabled
 # default feature=auto see meson_options.txt
 COMP_ARGS+=-Dselinux=disabled
 
+# gresource ELF inspection is optional; libelf is not a declared dependency.
+COMP_ARGS+=-Dlibelf=disabled
+
 # default boolean=true see meson_options.txt
 COMP_ARGS+=-Dglib_assert=false
 
